# Tangerine positive canary manifest — the authority for tests/canary/.
#
# This manifest is the bootstrap acceptance gate for the positive native
# canary suite. The harness (scripts/bootstrap_helpers.sh) enforces parity in
# BOTH directions:
#   - every file listed below MUST exist in tests/canary/   (absence is fatal)
#   - every file in tests/canary/ MUST be listed below      (no unlisted tests)
#   - the discovered set == the manifest set == the count   (exact, no drift)
#   - a zero/missing suite or manifest is fatal             (never "0/0 passed")
#
# Format: one filename.tg per line (relative to tests/canary/). Blank lines
# and lines starting with '#' are ignored. The '# count:' line is REQUIRED:
# it must equal both the number of listed entries and the harness's recorded
# expected count (CANARY_SUITE_POSITIVE_COUNT). Adding a canary means adding
# it here AND bumping '# count:' AND the harness constant together.
#
# The critical pre-self-host subset (run_critical_canaries) is a SUBSET of
# this manifest; every critical canary must be a member listed here.
#
# count: 75
# suite: positive canaries (access_*, resource_*, set_*, sink_*, deinit_*,
#        capability_*, generic-ownership, runtime/ABI surfaces)
# suite totals (positive + negative + arm64): 75 + 56 + 2 = 133

